1
00:00:00,801 --> 00:00:04,401
Sept 8, 2025: one npm maintainer, qix, was phished.

2
00:00:05,216 --> 00:00:09,416
19 packages, 2.71 billion downloads the week before. Are we hit?

3
00:00:09,332 --> 00:00:12,932
PatientZero answers from a FalkorDB graph of our 22 services.

4
00:00:14,816 --> 00:00:19,216
Red means the range on the last edge admits the malicious version.

5
00:00:20,732 --> 00:00:24,132
Six hand-written Cypher queries, answered in milliseconds.

6
00:00:26,469 --> 00:00:30,469
Every chain ends in an npm semver check on the last edge.

7
00:00:32,745 --> 00:00:37,345
Honest negatives: checkout-api reaches debug, but its range excludes the bad version.

8
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:44,265
Direct dependencies only: 1 service. Transitive depth is the whole story.

9
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:51,388
14 of the 19 compromised packages are reachable from this fleet.

10
00:00:52,352 --> 00:00:55,552
Every cell in the matrix is a path in the graph.

11
00:00:57,301 --> 00:01:00,501
Owning team and on-call for every exposed service, from the graph.

12
00:01:03,642 --> 00:01:08,242
Overrides pinned to clean versions, one draft per team. Written back to FalkorDB.

13
00:01:09,201 --> 00:01:12,601
A human approves the plan; it is remembered as a playbook.

14
00:01:15,343 --> 00:01:17,943
Ask again, in one word.

15
00:01:20,421 --> 00:01:24,621
Answered from graph memory, citing the incident and when.

16
00:01:26,550 --> 00:01:30,950
Compromise, advisories, our incident and the approved playbook, as dated nodes.

17
00:01:31,683 --> 00:01:34,283
Bring your own repo: its real dependency graph, in a separate FalkorDB graph.

18
00:01:35,731 --> 00:01:39,131
axios: exposed at runtime through https-proxy-agent, then debug.

19
00:01:43,732 --> 00:01:48,132
Express 4 pins debug 2.6.9 exactly, so its runtime was clean.

20
00:01:48,157 --> 00:01:54,757
The same tools over MCP: a real client gets the same 13 of 22.

21
00:01:55,270 --> 00:01:59,500
Deterministic first. The LLM only when needed, name-checked, with hard spend caps.
